{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QdK3DbmnvwmMSTm3tphDmJ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== RUN   TestZZProbe\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"  # of cases on Linux <!-- note --> only.\": limits=0 problems=[\"accepted limits: the section holds an HTML comment marker; write the limits without comments\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"<!-- c --> # only on Linux.\": limits=0 problems=[\"accepted limits: the section holds an HTML comment marker; write the limits without comments\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"#<!----> of cases only on Linux.\": limits=1 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"#<!-- c --> of cases only on Linux.\": limits=1 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"###<!-- c --> only on Linux.\": limits=1 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"# of cases <!-- note --> only on Linux.\": limits=1 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:12: long: [\"accepted limits: - L1 a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a …\" \"accepted limit L2 is not sealed: part of it could not be read\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:12: long: [\"accepted limits: a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long …\" \"accepted limit L2 is not sealed: part of it could not be read\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:12: long: [\"accepted limits: - nested a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption word a long assumption wor…\" \"accepted limit L2 is not sealed: part of it could not be read\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:13: prior: limits=0 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:13: prior: limits=0 problems=[]\n    zz_probe_test.go:13: prior: limits=0 problems=[\"accepted limits: an unterminated HTML comment hides the rest of the spec\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:13: prior: limits=0 problems=[]\nREPO 2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md [{\"L1\" \"The limits are written by the implementer, so a limit can be broader than it should be. Accepted because the brief presents them as data to verify and a disputed limit is a blocking finding of its own.\" \"\"} {\"L2\" \"A spec edited after sealing changes its limits only through a new bundle. Accepted because the limits enter the plan digest, so an edit stales the review as any other change does.\" \"\"}] []\nREPO 2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md [{\"L1\" \"A Git command the engine runs through another constructor, or a tool a validation step runs, can still refresh the index. Accepted because every engine read goes through `gitCommandContext`, and what a step runs is the project's command, which the Harne8 bugfix of its own scripts already covers.\" \"\"} {\"L2\" \"Outside Linux there is no anonymous memory file, so a diff reads a private copy of the index in a temporary directory, which a dry run there w\nREPO 2026-11-25-pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout.md [{\"L1\" \"The path is derived from the temporary directory of the process that dispatches, so a resume run with another `TMPDIR` recreates the checkout elsewhere and the session meets the old failure. Accepted because the dispatcher's environment is the operator's and the failure is the same one this spec removes for the usual case, a resume from the same shell.\" \"\"} {\"L2\" \"The path is predictable, so another local user can create it first and block the \nREPO 2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md [{\"L1\" \"A recorded runtime name is a path component taken from the run ledger, which the repository holds. Accepted because only names of the form `pose-review-run-<1–40 letters or digits>` are used, always below the temporary directory, and the directory is still created exclusively and never followed.\" \"\"}] []\nREPO 2026-11-26-pose-validate-read-only-index-followups.md [{\"L1\" \"In a split-index repository a read touches the modification time of `.git/sharedindex.<hash>`. Accepted because Git freshens the shared index on every read (measured on 2026-11-26: `git status` and `git ls-files` with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` both move it), so no engine read can avoid it, and the file's bytes do not change.\" \"\"}] []\nREPO 2026-11-27-pose-review-resume-residuals.md [{\"L1\" \"Some guards have no failing test: an lstat error other than not-exist counting as held, a continued round whose ledger read fails, the winner's record or the refused replan returned after a claim-publication conflict, the plans' own recorded-continuation returns and kind rules, and the plans' waits, which run without the dispatch's context for up to two seconds. Accepted because each needs a permission or ledger fault, or a race inside a plan the hooks do not \nREPO 2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md [{\"L1\" \"The review history ledger passing its own deadline to the index lookup has no failing test. Accepted because observing it needs a stand-in Git that outlasts the ledger's 30 s deadline, and the lookup is bounded by its own 30 s otherwise, so a regression changes the bound, not the outcome.\" \"\"}] []\n--- PASS: TestZZProbe (0.02s)\nPASS\nok  \tgithub.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/pose\t0.025s\n---- OLD\n=== RUN   TestZZProbe\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"  # of cases on Linux <!-- note --> only.\": limits=0 problems=[\"accepted limits: the section holds an HTML comment marker; write the limits without comments\"]\n    zz_probe_test.go:9: \"<!-- c --> # only on Linux.\": limits=0 problems=[\"accepted limits: