iew_bundle.go\",\"line\":3186,\"summary\":\"The doc comment of PreflightReviewAttestation still says it returns the reasons the writer would refuse an approving attestation, although it now also refuses non-approving ones.\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R1-N1\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe: both reported cases (indented heading with comment, leading comment) now yield 0 limits and the comment-marker problem; TestAHeadingRevealedByACommentDoesNotCloseTheSection passes. A narrower variant with a comment glued to the hash still seals a cut limit and is filed as N9.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:222 applies TruncateUTF8 at 300 bytes to every problem on each return path through boundProblems; TestAcceptedLimitProblemsAreBoundedInSize passes. The loss of the reason it introduces is N10.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay CLI probe: attest of changes-requested within-limit L9 now exits 1 both without and with --apply with the same blocker; a changes-requested open finding exits 0 in both. PreflightReviewAttestation at review_bundle.go:3192 is shared with the MCP preview; the error text says attestation. Remaining stale comment filed as N11.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N4\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe: ### Accepted --> limits still yields 0 limits and no problem; recorded as an open spec follow-up.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N5\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe: a tab-indented backtick block still yields 0 limits and no problem; recorded as an open spec follow-up.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe: a list-nested four-space fence holding a comment opener still refuses as unterminated where the base parser sealed 1 limit; recorded as an open spec follow-up.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"The Technical risks line of the spec now states that a comment opener in a span continued over lines can hide what follows, as the earlier engine did, matching the probe; the behaviour itself is an open spec follow-up.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N8\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"git diff 1487b003..7ee50f0b: the htmlCommentStart doc no longer describes the odd-backtick rule and the acceptedLimitsAndProblemsOf doc no longer names acceptedLimitsOf.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"Swept the whole subject at 7ee50f0b: the accepted limits parser and its round 2 diff, probed against the base parser for heading, comment, long-line, tab, list-fence and multi-line span cases; every spec under .pose/specs parsed by both (no change in limits or problems); attestation writer, CLI preview, MCP preview path and error text; run conclusion legacy derivation (unchanged since round 1); new and changed tests; spec text and follow-ups; manual wording. Ran focused tests, go vet of the two packages and the planned pose tools other than validate and the two post-review gates.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Parsing and admission logic only; no new shared state or lifecycle.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Preview and write now agree for an unsealed limit; the error wording change has no matcher in code or docs searched.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N10\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-approval-domain-preflight-integration\",\"rationale\":\"CLI and MCP share the preflight and writer; the CLI preview and apply were probed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N10\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined repository specs with the base and new parser: identical limits and problems. A non-approving attestation with an open finding previews and records as before. R6 and the error wording are the declared or review-driven changes; the parser residual is reported as N9.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N10\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N10\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N10\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"Examined change set cs-318e5be12a1a and the round 2 diff against R1-R8 and D1: each hunk serves a requirement or a round 1 finding, and the remaining gaps are recorded as spec follow-ups.\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N9\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"rationale\":\"The round 2 fixes are a prefix guard, a truncation with an existing helper and a reuse of unsealedLimitBlockers in the preflight; no new dependency or extension point. Their placement defects are reported as N9 and N10. D1 stays valid while a later derivation changes only the sealed-limit check.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-limits-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; orphan warnings shown.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-fa32940a7c8a474b\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, with no structural delta.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"asses